
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# One line. Start it with one of these seven words.
#
#   added:      something new you can use
#   changed:    something that already existed and now works differently
#   fixed:      a bug gone
#   removed:    something taken away
#   ---- the four above go in the CHANGELOG. The three below don't: ----
#   internal:   refactoring, tests, cleanups
#   docs:       README, SECURITY, man page, comments
#   packaging:  build-deb.sh, icons, .desktop, dependencies
#
# Write it as if finishing the sentence "From this commit on...".
#   added: LaTeX export
#   fixed: cover preview was blurry on HiDPI screens
#   internal: reworked the PDF writer
#
# Rules:
#   - one commit, one thing. If you need the word "and", that's two commits.
#   - lowercase after the colon, no full stop.
#   - keep the line under 72 characters.
#   - if the WHY needs saying, leave a blank line and say it below.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
